WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.150
It is the middle of the
night in a gurdwara.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.560
A reader's voice fills the hall.

3
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.870
A few people sit and listen.

4
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.190
Beside the reader, the next
one waits to take over.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.100
This reading began almost two days ago.

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:19.450
It will not pause until
all 1,430 pages are read.

7
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.710
So why would people read
a book aloud for two days,

8
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.640
without a single pause?

9
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.040
In this mission, you'll see
how an Akhand Path begins,

10
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.120
keeps going, and ends.

11
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.330
Then you'll find out when Sikhs hold one,

12
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.440
and why it matters to Sikhs.

13
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:41.040
Your mission: find out why Sikhs read a
1,430-page book aloud for two days without

14
00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:42.270
a single pause.
